{"data":{"title":"The Offbeat","slug":"the-offbeat","path":"/artists/flyamsam/tracks/the-offbeat/","artwork":"images/artists/flyamsam/tracks/the-offbeat.jpg","artist":{"id":"12F7OWJbupk","slug":"flyamsam","links":null,"title":"FLYamSAM","artwork":null},"id":"WccFd7iq698"},"appearanceCount":5,"markers":[{"chapter":{"id":"YPAS1SwTpMY","show":{"id":"XuyBzFgMCMI","slug":"516","title":"Soulection Radio Show #516","artwork":"images/episodes/soulection-radio-show-516.jpg","content":"Laid back grooves from Kamaal Williams, J Dilla and Lucy Pearl.\n<!--more-->\n","published_at":"2021-08-07T00:00:00+00:00"}}},{"chapter":{"id":"UQKUtJsffKA","show":{"id":"cdnqQ9xehXc","slug":"195","title":"Soulection Radio Show #195","artwork":"/images/episodes/195.jpg","content":"Joe Kay continues the freestyle of all music. \n\n<!--more-->\nLast week's show was definitely one of my favorites to date. It's weird how things work. It's the shows that I feel most unprepared for that end up doing well... maybe it's because I just really freestyle and go off of my whole library of music rather than trying to curate a specific vibe. It was hard to top last week's show but I did my best to really take it right back to the early beat era from 2008-2012 and played some current gems as well. I hope you enjoy this. I'll be back next week with a guest maybe.\n\nBless.\n\n\nThanks to [true listener^^](https://soundcloud.com/true_listener) for supplying this tracklist.\n","published_at":"2014-11-29T00:00:00+00:00"}}},{"chapter":{"id":"8lwnXcRS0XE","show":{"id":"QwKXMkdRTEM","slug":"251","title":"Soulection Radio Show #251 (The People's Choice)","artwork":"/images/episodes/251.jpg","content":"\n<!--more-->\n\n","published_at":"2016-03-19T00:00:00+00:00"}}},{"chapter":{"id":"rBTjD90b6NE","show":{"id":"gXo3AqS_FMA","slug":"339","title":"Soulection Radio Show #339 (Live from Melbourne, Australia)","artwork":"/images/episodes/339.jpg","content":"\n<!--more-->\n\n","published_at":"2017-12-09T00:00:00+00:00"}}},{"